Z||000000||recluse||08-13-2001||05:51 PM||||I trimed down the intake tube that runs from the factory air box to the throttle body (v6)<BR>and mounted a cone type filter to the end of it and "pointed" it to the toward the opening after removing the factory air box.  While this works, i could not notice any performance gain and i just dont like it, for one thing, the filter is next to the exhaust pipe so it is probably just sucking hot air. I have a set of the panel type scoops but hav'nt installed them yet.  Once i do i would like to get the filter right next to the scoop for more air.  Has anyone else came up with a better system??  And has anyone bought the intake tube and filter from the Fiero Store?  IF so how did it work?  I just cant see spending that much on one.  Any info would be great, pics would be great too...  THanks<P>Matt 87 GT||||reg||5
