Z||000004||Primaris||08-13-2001||10:01 PM||||I know those cone filters are all the rage, but I don't see how you could get more air using one in the fiero.  The Fiero already has an outside the engine bay intake (cold air).  And the box behind the quarter panel flows very freely.  I'd just buy a K & N filter and drop it in.  The only think that might help is adding a holly type ram scoop.<P>------------------<BR>Signatures are a waste of bandwidth!||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||08-13-2001||10:36 PM||||Unless you are flowing more than 180 gm/s of air, you won't see any cosmic difference. The V6 is good for about 150 gm/s at best. With the shields installed on the crossover pipe there is some temperature rise in the incoming air, but nothing horrifying.||||reg||1
